 "constraints": [],
 "stem": "In an arithmetic sequence with the first term ${=a}$ and the common difference ${=d}$, find how many terms from the first term sum up to ${=S}$.",
 "answer": "N",
 "solution": [
  "$a={=a}$, $d={=d}$ and $S_n={=S}$.",
  "$S_n=\\frac12n\\{2a+(n-1)d\\}$, so ${=S}=\\frac12n\\{{=2*a}+(n-1)\\times{=d}\\}$.",
  "Multiply out: ${=d}n^2+{=2*a-d}n-{=2*S}=0$.",
  "Solving gives $n={=N}$ or $n={=o}$.",
  "$n$ must be a natural number, so $n={=N}$."
 ],
 "notes": "Basic: positive a and d so the second root is always negative; one quadratic, mirrors warm-up-8."
}
